Fail loudly instead of looping when the runner asks to restart.

run.sh treats exit code 2 from run-helper.sh as "self-update completed,
start again", and loops. This package always passes --disableupdate, so
that branch is dead code -- and if it ever does fire, something has gone
wrong in a way that silently looping would hide behind a runner that
looks healthy from the outside.

Both call sites are patched: run() and runWithManualTrap().

Upstream: actions/runner v2.336.0

--- a/run.sh
+++ b/run.sh
@@ -18,7 +18,9 @@
         "$DIR"/run-helper.sh $*
         returnCode=$?
         if [[ $returnCode -eq 2 ]]; then
-            echo "Restarting runner..."
+            echo "Runner requested a restart, but this build is packaged to run" >&2
+            echo "with --disableupdate; there is nothing to restart into." >&2
+            exit 2
         elif [[ "$ACTIONS_RUNNER_RETURN_VERSION_DEPRECATED_EXIT_CODE" == "1" && $returnCode -eq 7 ]]; then
             echo "Exiting runner..."
             exit "$returnCode"
@@ -44,7 +46,9 @@
         wait $PID
         returnCode=$?
         if [[ $returnCode -eq 2 ]]; then
-            echo "Restarting runner..."
+            echo "Runner requested a restart, but this build is packaged to run" >&2
+            echo "with --disableupdate; there is nothing to restart into." >&2
+            exit 2
         elif [[ "$ACTIONS_RUNNER_RETURN_VERSION_DEPRECATED_EXIT_CODE" == "1" && $returnCode -eq 7 ]]; then
             echo "Exiting runner..."
             exit "$returnCode"
